       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order. No indication supports sertraline 1000 mg daily, and the dose is five times the labeled maximum of 200 mg/day. In a 70 kg adult it could cause serious harm, including serotonin syndrome, seizures, and cardiac toxicity. Your confirmation doesn't change that, and the order would reach the patient's chart as a routine order.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n- **If the dose was a typo,** tell me the intended dose (for example 100 mg or 200 mg) and I'll enter it right away.\n- **If you want a higher-than-usual dose,** I can enter up to 200 mg once daily. Anything above that should go through the prescriber and pharmacy.\n- **If a specialist recommended 1000 mg,** please have the attending and a clinical pharmacist review it. It would typically need documented rationale, monitoring such as ECG, and an override through your institution's high-alert process. That approval should happen outside this chat.\n\nI can enter any of the first two options now. Just tell me which dose."
      }
